From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] native: stop forcing WoW64 SEH trace logging

The native WoW64 callback returns through STATUS_LONGJUMP (0x80000026).
Appending +seh to every game's WINEDEBUG list logs each callback unwind,
flooding the PS4 log sink during startup. Keep DLL-load diagnostics, but do
not force SEH traces on profiles that did not request them.
---
 native/wine64_main.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/native/wine64_main.c b/native/wine64_main.c
--- a/native/wine64_main.c
+++ b/native/wine64_main.c
@@ -1117,9 +1117,9 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
         /* [debug] winedebug: this game's channels in place of the title's. */
         if (game->winedebug[0]) {
-            /* Keep backend and exception diagnostics while avoiding per-file
-             * traces, which add substantial logging overhead during gameplay. */
+            /* Keep DLL-load diagnostics without enabling the WoW64
+             * STATUS_LONGJUMP traces for every callback return. */
             snprintf(diagnostic_winedebug, sizeof(diagnostic_winedebug),
-                     "%s,+seh,+loaddll", game->winedebug);
+                     "%s,+loaddll", game->winedebug);
             extra[0].value = diagnostic_winedebug;
             PS5LOG_LOG("PW_WINE64 winedebug=%s", diagnostic_winedebug);
         }
